{"content":{"activity_type":"event_msg/item_completed","completed_at_ms":1790978508962,"item":{"aggregated_output":"[{\"body\":\"Capture conversations from the selected 20 coding CLIs. Known text is retained in annals, binary payloads become references, and unknown native records remain visible as drift evidence. Cursor uses native hooks plus an optional headless stream-JSON wrapper; Kiro uses V3 hooks and a watched launcher for default V2 sessions.\\n\\nReal installed TUI sessions exposed capture and verification bugs. OpenHands now installs native session-start, prompt-submission and pre/post-tool hooks alongside turn-end hooks, so submitted prompts survive a stalled model request. An installed-TUI regression holds the first model request open and requires automatic prompt capture before any response, exit or backfill; hosted CI runs it on macOS and Linux. The Cline follower waits for the interactive session's final manifest. Cline/Copilot drivers wait for completed assistant output and inspect follower completion before exporting evidence. Copilot drift checks use its producer ID. The PTY helper optionally exposes bounded live terminal traces for inspecting real startup/approval screens.\\n\\n**Live canary evidence:** 18 of the 20 selected CLIs passed installed interactive TUI sessions on macOS: Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, Copilot, Qwen, Kiro, Mistral Vibe, Cline, Goose, Aider, Continue, Kilo, Droid, OpenCode, Pi, Crush, OpenHands and Open Interpreter. Passes require the human prompt, successful linked file-read result, answer containing the synthetic file text and normal exit, captured automatically before manual backfill. The latest five retests used local DeepSeek with bounded requests and zero paid usage. OpenHands additionally captured its prompt before any model reply, retained default tool approvals and resumed the same conversation for one exact benign read approval. Interpreter uses its verified native/chat compatibility route. Prior blocked attempts and model/driver limitations are preserved in [sanitized evidence](docs/verification-evidence); [the live matrix](docs/LIVE_VERIFICATION.md) distinguishes these from headless results. Cursor's interactive native transcript lacks tool-result bodies; Kimi's explicitly authorized native folder-trust prompt was accepted in its real TUI; automatic prompt/Read call/result/session-state capture and normal exit passed, but the guard rejected a second request while the first stream remained active; the first stream later timed out. This is a harness stream-sequencing gap, not established provider failure. No retry or manual backfill was attempted. These are canary smoke passes, not complete certification of every input type, lifecycle or Linux live-provider behavior.\\n\\n**Free CI:** installs pinned real binaries on both operating systems and drives 18 headless and 17 interactive scenarios against scripted local providers. Account-gated Droid is a loud `blocked: login-required` warning in its empty CI profile; missing login never counts as coverage or qualifies a pin update. Its real BYOK TUI passed using existing account authentication. [Hosted run 37057118602](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/actions/runs/37057118602) passed on both systems at commit `9842af0`: each recorded 18 headless and 17 interactive passes, one explicit Droid login blocker and zero failures. Each regression suite recorded 343 tests, 330 passes and 13 explicit opt-in skips; the installed stalled-prompt check separately passed with zero skips. Crush submits Enter independently of repainted prompt echoes. A subsequent documentation-triggered rerun exposed an OpenHands rendered-answer matcher flake on Linux. Its quit action now waits for bounded read-only observation of the existing automatic capture gates, including linked result/answer/session/Stop records and no drift; local installed TUI checks passed twice. The new hosted rerun is pending. PTY cleanup has a forced deadline and stalled-test ledger polling runs in bounded children; required evidence gates and pass counts remain unchanged.\\n\\nFortnightly maintenance remains review-first and spends no inference credits. After merge it observes releases and prepares draft pin-update PRs; candidate packages run without write credentials and must pass headless and interactive verification. A separate job validates the exact proposal before publishing. Repository PR creation is enabled, default workflow permission is read-only and auto-merge is off. The local scheduler remains available as an alternative.\\n\\nPaid live-provider CI is not enabled or implemented. A future manual-dispatch tier requires explicit CLI/model approval, a sole key-holding proxy with request/token limits, and durable atomic monthly accounting or provider hard budgets to enforce the $5 per-CLI ceiling across runs. [The cost split](docs/LIVE_VERIFICATION.md#cost-and-execution-tiers) records this requirement. The free scheduled tier never receives paid credentials.\\n\\n[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) documents setup, fixture/repository tests, installed headless/TUI smoke, live-provider checks, broader record/lifecycle verification, release-update review, and adding a new CLI. Features should cover all applicable CLIs, with linked issues for uncovered integrations. The README links the guide; commands were checked against the actual verifier entrypoints.\\n\",\"number\":26,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Expand CLI capture and isolated native verification\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-02T21:24:46Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/26\"},{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n- Document the sibling annals checkout and installation order required by the local dependency, plus Node.js 20 minimum.\\n- Correct the technical design: legacy inspect --force cannot bypass the agent-session refusal.\\n\\n## Verification\\n- Checked installation instructions against package engines, dependency paths, and prepare scripts.\