naries, install cledger capture into\\n+disposable profiles, and launch interactive sessions on macOS and Linux. Never\\n+inherit normal credentials, sessions or hooks. Build provider configuration\\n+explicitly after creating the isolated environment. Use a scripted HTTP model\\n+substitute in free CI; local canaries accept contributor-configured endpoint,\\n+model and protocol instead of assuming DeepSeek. Paid checks remain a separate\\n+explicit tier with enforced budgets.\\n+\\n+Raw PTY markers are partial rendering evidence. Full screen-layout evaluation,\\n+including possible image-based checks, remains deferred. For now inspect markers,\\n+tool rows, import disclosure and render failures; separately inspect outbound\\n+provider requests and automatic ledger observations before any backfill.\\n+\\n+## Implementation sequence\\n+\\n+1. Establish matrix, report validation and portable PTY isolation (initial foundation).\\n+2. Add installed scripted-provider bridge drivers for the three hubs, including\\n+   continuation, resume and lineage. Replace the old smoke test's writes to normal\\n+   user session stores. Keep legacy smoke explicitly separate from certification.\\n+3. Add Gemini and Qwen targets, then remaining roster targets. Model native resume,\\n+   native import and bootstrap as independent capabilities with version evidence.\\n+   Validate content changes introduced by cledger attachment-reference retention.\\n+4. Provision and run both-OS CI, expanding hub routes incrementally. Publish\\n+   reports with explicit unimplemented/blocked cells and local/provider exclusions.\\n+5. Add fortnightly review-first maintenance: observe roster/releases, provision\\n+   candidate versions, require installed interactive verification before advancing\\n+   pins, and prepare draft PRs. No auto-merge. Existing drift reporting remains\\n+   active until the replacement has meaningful installed verification gates.\\n+\\n+Current adapters' broad validated version pr